# sunshine-ds (desktop GameStream)

Two servers: Decky Flatpak `:47989` (KMS) and Distrobox sunshine-ds `:48100` (`capture = kwin`). Pin Thor/Odin Moonlight to `:48100` on Plasma. Dual-stream is Plasma/KWin only.

Game Mode dual-stream is a **third** server: `sunshine-ds-kms` `:48200` (`capture = kms`, `dual_display_source = gamescope-virtual`). Checkpoint `checkpoint-2026-09-10-gamemode-works`. Recipe: `.cursor/skills/sunshine-ds-gamemode/SKILL.md`. Sunshine x360 is **15-button** libvirtualhid (`LB=b6` `Back=b10`); do not write Steam xpad 11-button maps.

- `pgrep -x sunshine-ds` / `pgrep -x sunshine-ds-kms` only. Never `pgrep -f` / `pkill -f` sunshine. Never put `sunshine-ds-virtual-output` in a `pgrep -f` pattern; kill leftover helpers by numeric PID.
- Exactly one long-lived `sunshine-ds-virtual-output --name sunshine-ds` at 1920×1080 during Plasma dual-stream. `--stop` kills it before Game Mode.
- Game Mode video/1 is headless gamescope on `:2`, not that KWin helper. Sidecar `$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/sunshine-ds-gamemode-virtual` must write `serial=` + `pw_node=` (not `node=`). Capture is object.serial + AUTOCONNECT. `--start-kms` when `:2` is already up — `--start` can KillMode the helper.
- Do not replace Decky Sunshine, `POST /api/restart`, `sudo systemctl --user`, or `kwin_wayland --replace`. Compositor `reinitialize` is last-resort for an all-black KWin FBO (kills the helper).
- Do not use `kscreen-doctor` to decide if `Virtual-sunshine-ds` exists (hangs with duplicates).
- Plasma dual-screen: standalone Flatpak Cemu/Azahar, never RetroDECK `-f`. Game Mode Cemu is RetroDECK windowed (`CEMU_GAMEMODE_DS=1`, no `-f`) via `ensure-cemu-gamemode-dual-screen.sh`. Cemu type is Wii U GamePad. GamePad inject searches `:1` then `:0` (never `:2` / `$DISPLAY`). HDMI / top taps use the same `:1`-first search onto Cemu TV (display 0 only; not Odin GamePad-only). Azahar is Separate Windows + `QT_QPA_PLATFORM=xcb`. Bind with `scripts/bind-gamepad.py`. Default `GAMESTREAM_PAD_PROFILE=x360`.
- Bring-up: `scripts/ensure-sunshine-ds.sh`. Return to Game Mode: Desktop shortcut or `scripts/switch-to-game-mode.sh`.
- Debug: `.cursor/skills/sunshine-ds-gamestream/SKILL.md`. Game Mode: `.cursor/skills/sunshine-ds-gamemode/SKILL.md`. Stack/SHAs: `.cursor/skills/sunshine-ds-gamestream/reference.md`.
